        "raw": "<p><em>Hey, I'm interjecting myself into this newb's post to remind you that, while not Christmas, the next best holiday has me! The best Hero, <strong>Guise!&nbsp;</strong>You better make this the best Halloween and use my cards. And dress up as me! I demand pics! Now 'scuse me while me and the others ding-dong ditch on this kooky old spook's hidden temple...</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Err, not sure what happened there but I guess I get to start off the Weekly One-Shot thread?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Challenge Trickster Kismet vs Dark Watch Setback, Completionist Guise, Luminary,&nbsp;Mainstay: Road Warrior&nbsp;and Akash'Thyria at The Temple of Zhu Long.&nbsp;<strong>With randomized start!</strong>&nbsp;How much candy can you get before you're knocked out? Spoilers below.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mint at 1/18/12/8/8 with swaps to regular Setback, regular Guise and Spirit of the Void Akash.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Practice showed this would require a methodical approach. Rites of Revival will be around in case a Hero is incapacitated, although Challenge Trickster Kismet means you want Hero targets or the Environment to remove your Devices &amp; Seeds, because if Kismet does she will play out more of her deck in a hard hitting loop. Getting reduction out can also help mitigate damage and mind what side Kismet is flipped to when the Jinxes stack up.</p>",
